# Documentation

A class and a domain model are documented the same way. Each has a short English docstring. Each public attribute and each public method has one too.

- Say what it is or what it returns, and when the value is empty.
- Do not retell the implementation. A docstring that lists the steps, names the query, or repeats the code is noise.
- One or two sentences. Skip private helpers.
- The class or method docstring is the first statement in the body. An attribute docstring is the string on the next line.

```python
# Bad: the docstring walks the steps
class Campaigns:
    """Loads rows, drops tombstones, and sorts by created_at."""

    def list(self) -> list[Campaign]:
        """Runs a select, skips deleted_at, and maps each row."""
        ...

# Good
class Campaign:
    """A campaign stored for this tracker."""

    name: str
    """Name shown to the operator. Empty before the campaign is named."""

    def renamed(self, name: str) -> Campaign:
        """This campaign under another name."""
        ...
```
